      "id": "e9d7aed3213b6f06fe29",
      "name": "mpfi",
      "epoch": "0",
      "version": "1.5.4",
      "release": "11.fc44",
      "architecture": "amd64",
      "summary": "An interval arithmetic library based on MPFR",
      "description": "MPFI is intended to be a portable library written in C for arbitrary precision\ninterval arithmetic with intervals represented using MPFR reliable\nfloating-point numbers.  It is based on the GNU MP library and on the MPFR\nlibrary and is part of the latter.  The purpose of an arbitrary precision\ninterval arithmetic is on the one hand to get \"guaranteed\" results, thanks to\ninterval computation, and on the other hand to obtain accurate results, thanks\nto multiple precision arithmetic.  The MPFI library is built upon MPFR in\norder to benefit from the correct roundings provided by MPFR.  Further\nadvantages of using MPFR are its portability and compliance with the IEEE 754\nstandard for floating-point arithmetic.",
      "homepage": "https://perso.ens-lyon.fr/nathalie.revol/software.html",
      "license": "LGPL-3.0-or-later AND LGPL-2.1-or-later",
